  be anything for example an e-commerce  company will convince you to purchase  some of their stored products  now let's talk about the copywriting  formula a good copy usually follows aida  formula a stands for attention i for  interest d for desire and a for action  almost every good copywriter uses this  formula to write better copies and it's  important for you in case you decided to  become a copywriter or want to use  copywriting in some of your work so i  hope now we understand what actually  copywriting is now let's try to  understand what does a copywriter  actually do  the copywriter's job is to write words  that convince an audience to take some  action for the benefit of the company in  which the writer works  let's have a look at sample copyrighted  job description that will help you  understand the role and responsibilities  and the skills needed for this role  so firstly let's have a look at  responsibilities writing editing and  publishing engaging content for various  social media network including facebook  twitter instagram linkedin and google my  business optimizing social media post  language tone message based on your  target audience behavior selecting  appealing images and videos to  complement text for designers to design  the post  let's have a look at some more  responsibilities coordinate with  internal teams to create advertising  posts for client respond to questions  and comments on social media pages  promptly and accurately  there can be more responsibilities to a  copywriter depending on what the company  needs so it varies from company to  company now let's see what skills a  company looks for in a copywriter  hands-on experience using various social  media platform to advertise solid  knowledge of seo keyword research and  analytics tools example google analytics  familiarity with online paid advertising  let's have a look of some others  requirement and skills  ability to deliver creative web content  text image and video excellent  communication skills  so now we know what copywriter does  let's explore its various types  seo copywriting it means optimizing the  copy using keywords to make it rank at  the top of the search results for  example if you optimize a company's  product page correctly through seo  copywriting then there is a high chances  that your sales page would rank at the  top of the search result which would  result in more sales next we have social  media copywriting this type of  copywriting is used on social media  platform for example a catchy title is  used to grab the attention of the user  and emoji is used to make the copy  interesting or frame the right message  in order to convince the audience to  take some kind of action next we have  technical copywriting the motive for  writing technical copy is to explain the  latest technologies or the technical  product that a company wants to sell for  example if you have a tech product you  need a copywriter who can explain the  technical aspect use case of the product  and how that product helped the customer  direct response copywriting it is a type  of communication that is compelling  enough to be able to influence the  customers to act  in other words any copy that encourages  the recipient to act immediately and the  response from the reader are miserable  another type of copywriting is public  relation copywriting in public relation  copywriting you write newsworthy things  to catch your audience attention and  gain their trust it helps you quickly  earn an audience with credible sources  and as a result your business can  promote its product and services more  effectively whenever you search on  google you see some ads at the top of  the search results that are also made up  using copywriting following that next we  have ad copywriting this type of  copywriting is used to create effective  ads generally it's used in facebook and  google ads now we reached the second  last type of copywriting in the list  which is 